  "/hub/behind-the-gates-horse-rescue": `<main><article><p>Hawkez Haven Information Hub</p><h1>Behind the Gates of Hawkez Haven: The Raw Reality of Horse Rescue</h1><p>What horse rescue really involves — from the costs and consequences of irresponsible rehoming to the rehabilitation and responsibility that begin once a horse comes through the gates.</p><img src="/images/hero_image_hub.png" alt="Rescue horse at Hawkez Haven – Second Chances in New Zealand" width="1200" height="800" /><h2>When Horses Pay the Price</h2><p>Too many horses end up in crisis because of irresponsible sales and rehoming practices. Responsible horse sales are not just about transferring ownership; they are about taking responsibility for where that horse's life goes next.</p><h2>Money Doesn't Guarantee Welfare</h2><p>A high purchase price does not guarantee a good life. Rehabilitation can take months, specialised care and ongoing support.</p><h2>What Rescue Actually Inherits</h2><p>Horse rescue can involve emergency veterinary treatment, specialised medication, farrier care, hoof rehabilitation, dental care, nutrition, transport, safe housing, equipment and months or years of physical and behavioural rehabilitation.</p><h2>The Things People Don't Always See</h2><p>Responsible surrender matters, and Hawkez Haven is deeply grateful for people who help with transport, feed, equipment and other practical needs when they can no longer keep a horse.</p><h2>Rehoming Is a Responsibility</h2><p>Responsible rehoming means asking questions, checking references, inspecting the property, assessing financial readiness and planning for what happens if circumstances change.</p><h2>The Cost Doesn't Disappear</h2><p>When an owner or seller walks away without taking responsibility, those costs simply land somewhere else. Hawkez Haven absorbs them because the horse still needs care.</p><p>Every horse deserves the opportunity for a safe and meaningful second chance at life.</p><p><a href="/hub">Back to The Hub</a> · <a href="/hub/horse-adoption-nz">Horse Adoption Guide</a> · <a href="/support">Support Hawkez Haven</a></p></article></main>`,
  "/hub/horse-adoption-nz": { title: "Horse Adoption NZ | How to Adopt a Rescue Horse", description: "Considering horse adoption in NZ? Learn how rescue horse adoption works, what to prepare, the costs involved, welfare responsibilities and how to find the right match." },
